# code-review-graph ignore rules — Realty Pandit
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
# The built-in DEFAULT_IGNORE_PATTERNS use anchored fnmatch patterns like "node_modules/**".
# fnmatch matches the WHOLE relative path, so "node_modules/**" only matches a node_modules
# directory at the repo ROOT. This repo keeps its dependencies nested --
# agents/backend/node_modules, agents/website/node_modules, agents/frontend/node_modules,
# agents/browser-qa/node_modules, agents/call-gateway/node_modules -- none of which matched.
# Result: the graph indexed all of them and graph.db reached 2.59 GB, which is what made
# code-review-graph stall sessions.
#
# The patterns below are unanchored (leading *) so they match at ANY depth.
# Do not "tidy" them into node_modules/** -- that is the bug.

# Dependencies (the 2.59 GB culprit)
*node_modules*

# Build output
*/dist/*
*/build/*
*/.next/*
*/out/*
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map

# Test / coverage / caches
*/coverage/*
*/.turbo/*
*/.cache/*
*/__pycache__/*
*/.pytest_cache/*
*/playwright-report/*
*/test-results/*

# Vendored tooling and binaries
*/platform-tools/*
*/.venv/*
*/venv/*
*.exe
*.dll
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.dump
*.sql

# Generated / data artifacts
*/.code-review-graph/*
*/prisma/migrations/*
*.db
*.sqlite
*.log

# Media
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.mp4
*.webm
*.pdf
